WEBVTT

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:01.960
Section ten.

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.570
Counterexamples and failure cases.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.860
Their purpose is to show where an apparently sensible

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.480
pipeline can mislead us.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:16.470
We keep the confusing evidence visible rather than explaining

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:18.330
only the clean success case.

00:00:27.687 --> 00:00:30.847
One fixture explicitly says it is not part of

00:00:30.847 --> 00:00:31.807
Helios or Orion.

00:00:33.677 --> 00:00:37.177
Lexical names still retrieve both Projects, but the saved

00:00:37.177 --> 00:00:41.857
classifier selects HTTP Clients and Python with neither Project.

00:00:43.407 --> 00:00:46.527
Another audit fixture genuinely supports two initiatives.

00:00:47.757 --> 00:00:49.657
The task must allow both.

00:00:51.127 --> 00:00:53.807
A forced single winner would change the meaning of

00:00:53.807 --> 00:00:54.467
organization.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:04.100
The full FastAPI profile contains its purpose statement, but

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:08.600
an uppercase title marker let documentation links occupy compact

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:08.980
slots.

00:01:10.495 --> 00:01:13.375
Retrieval could see evidence the generator did not receive.

00:01:14.631 --> 00:01:18.351
Metadata still supported the saved answer, Web APIs and

00:01:18.351 --> 00:01:18.751
Python.

00:01:19.426 --> 00:01:22.706
An earlier answer added unwanted secondary labels.

00:01:24.002 --> 00:01:28.282
Primary-only policy clarified the task, but reused cases cannot

00:01:28.282 --> 00:01:30.942
establish an independent causal improvement.

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:40.980
Empty, fork-only, and metadata-only cases need no-match or

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:41.980
uncertainty paths.

00:01:43.097 --> 00:01:45.777
Installation noise can introduce unrelated names.

00:01:47.014 --> 00:01:48.954
English extraction can miss other languages.

00:01:49.231 --> 00:01:53.811
Narrow cleaning can miss malicious instructions or secret-like

00:01:53.811 --> 00:01:54.131
text.

00:01:55.208 --> 00:01:58.628
These fixtures explore boundaries; they are not a comprehensive

00:01:58.628 --> 00:01:59.768
security benchmark.

00:02:00.905 --> 00:02:04.105
Next, we preserve the decisions and uncertainty that follow

00:02:04.105 --> 00:02:05.005
from these cases.
